# Auth, link codes & notifications — invariants

Do not regress these when editing the files above. Details in
[docs/FIREBASE_BACKEND.md](../../docs/FIREBASE_BACKEND.md).

## Registration order

- In `AuthService.register()`, resolve the teacher link code **before**
  `createUserWithEmailAndPassword`. Creating the auth account first and then
  hitting an invalid code leaves an orphaned account whose email can't be
  reused.

## Link-code resolution is server-side

- Students resolve codes through the `resolveLinkCode` Cloud Function
  (`functions/index.js`), called from `TeacherLinkCodeService.resolveTeacherId`
  via `cloud_functions`. Do **not** reintroduce a direct Firestore read of
  `teacher_link_codes` for resolution — it must work pre-sign-in and must not
  expose the collection.
- `teacher_link_codes` rules deny anonymous reads; a teacher may read only
  their own code docs (and non-existent candidates while generating). Code
  generation in `ensureLinkCode` treats a permission-denied read as "taken."

## Notifications are staff-only writes

- Clients cannot write to `notifications` (rules require staff). Registration
  notifications are created by the `onUserCreated` Firestore trigger. Do not
  add client-side notification writes in the student registration flow.

## Progress ownership

- `student_progress` updates require the existing doc to already belong to the
  caller. Keep the ownership check on both create and update.

## After backend changes

- Deploy: `firebase deploy --only firestore:rules,functions` (Blaze plan).
